      "message": "Agreed that the native folio has to stay resident here: as for a native page in a `VM_LOCKED` VMA, a small folio is mlocked from its first slice PTE (aosp/4390444), and aosp/4367603 keeps one mlock reference per slice so that unlocking one slice doesn\u0027t make it evictable.\n\nAs far as I can see, though, no patch between aosp/4367986 and this one changes mlock. aosp/4367603 is already earlier in the chain, so the swapout step could never succeed, and with this change the subtest always skips. Could this be folded into aosp/4367986 (or into the reclaim test patch, if that one gets split out)?\n\nIf the stale-WP check is still worth having, could the fixture reach the swapped state without locking a sibling, for example by paging out the whole 16KB window before changing the registration? Otherwise, would it be OK to drop the subtest?",
